  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1999-p13.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Taking cube roots, \\(a_{n+1} = \\sqrt[3]{99}\\, a_n,\\) so the sequence is geometric with first term \\(1\\) and ratio \\(\\sqrt[3]{99}.\\) Then \\[ a_{100} = \\left(\\sqrt[3]{99}\\right)^{99} = 99^{33}. \\]\n\nThus, the correct answer is C.",
      "hints": [
        "Take cube roots: \\(a_{n+1} = \\sqrt[3]{99}\\, a_n\\)",
        "This is geometric with ratio \\(\\sqrt[3]{99},\\) so \\(a_{100} = (\\sqrt[3]{99})^{99}\\)"
      ],
